{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Basil","id":"339235123759153162","is_bot":0,"username":"divinedefault"},"author_id":"339235123759153162","channel_id":"715342330978238475","content":"Navars tears echo of a pain hundreds of years old and deeper than even this point of the ocean. he will be the last one to leave the chamber, only following after about 10 minutes. \n\"when it was done, and we carried the day, \nI watched her life's blood go slipping away. \nand I sat down, into her cold blue eyes-. \nsweet mother mary, deliver her grace. \ndeliver us all, from the look on her face and the screams, the long and desperate sighs.\n\nall our lives, have been a cruel secret.\nall our lives. a tender ancient bloom.\nso I drink this final cup.\nand I rest this weary head.\nand I watch the waters rising up\nto wash away the dead.\nand when we're rid of this disease\nand we have won the prize.\nI never will return to these, foreign skies.\"\n\nhe stands over the grave and places his sickle where he found the bracers. \"I will come back for you. If I can't hear your voice today, I will press on for what you loved. I will have a garden waiting for you\"","created_at":"2020-07-28T07:11:45.046000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"737567960134058114","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
